    "id": "AVIRIS-NG_ARCSIX_2024_2535_1",
    "stac_version": "1.1.0",
    "description": "This dataset contains Level 1B (L1B) calibrated radiance and Level 2A (L2A) orthocorrected surface reflectance products from the Airborne Visible / Infrared Imaging Spectrometer-Next Generation (AVIRIS-NG) instrument acquired between 2024-05-30 and 2024-08-16 for the Arctic Radiation-Cloud Aerosol-Surface Interaction Experiment (ARCSIX) project. ARCSIX was a NASA field investigation aimed at quantifying the contributions of surface properties, clouds, aerosol particles, and precipitation to the Arctic summer surface radiation budget and to sea ice melting during the early melt season. The L1B files include calibrated radiance. These data are georeferenced but not orthorectified; the L1B files include orthocorrected pixel locations in geographic coordinates and a geometric lookup table, which provides projected coordinates in a UTM grid. The L2A files hold orthocorrected surface hemispherical directional reflectance derived from calibrated radiance using an optimal estimation algorithm. These files include estimates of atmospheric aerosol optical thickness (AOT) and column water vapor. The L2A data are projected in a UTM coordinate system. The NASA AVIRIS-NG instrument is a pushbroom spectral mapping system with high signal-to-noise ratio (SNR), designed and toleranced for high-performance spectroscopy. AVIRIS-NG measures reflected radiance at 5-nm intervals in the Visible to Shortwave Infrared (VSWIR) spectral range from 380-2510 nm. The AVIRIS-NG sensor has a 1 milliradian instantaneous field of view, providing altitude dependent ground sampling distances from 20 m to sub meter range. AVIRIS-NG was flown on a NASA Gulfstream III aircraft. These AVIRIS-NG L1B and L2A data are provided in NetCDF format.",
